SneppX-ALG Installation
=======================

Prerequisites
  - C compiler: GCC 12+, Clang 15+, or MSVC 2022
  - C++20 compiler
  - CMake 3.16+ for direct configuration; 3.25+ for CMake presets
  - Python 3.11+ (optional, for Python bindings)
  - 4 GB RAM minimum
  - 2 GB free disk space
  - Linux, macOS, or Windows (WSL recommended on Windows)

Quick Install
  1. Clone the repository:
       git clone https://github.com/SneppX/sneppx-alg.git
       cd sneppx-alg

  2. Configure a release build:
       cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release

  3. Build:
       cmake --build build --config Release --parallel

  4. Run tests:
       cd build && ctest -C Release --output-on-failure

  5. To explicitly enable tests and benchmarks:
       cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DSNEPPX_BUILD_TESTS=ON -DSNEPPX_BUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON
       cmake --build build --config Release --parallel
       cd build && ctest -C Release --output-on-failure

Platform Notes
  Linux
    Install build-essential, CMake, and Ninja via your package manager.
    Example (Ubuntu/Debian):
      sudo apt-get install build-essential cmake ninja-build

  macOS
    Install Xcode Command Line Tools and CMake:
      xcode-select --install
      brew install cmake ninja

  Windows
    Native (MSVC):
      Install Visual Studio 2022 with "Desktop development with C++".
      Use a Developer Command Prompt and the CMake presets documented in
      docs/installation.md.

  Python Bindings (optional)
    Requires pybind11. Install it, then configure with:
      cmake -S . -B build-python -DSNEPPX_BUILD_PYTHON=ON
      cmake --build build-python --config Release --parallel

See docs/installation.md for detailed instructions, supported build options,
and platform-specific commands.
